From: OpenHarmony Build Team <build@openharmony.io>
Date: Sun, 25 May 2025 15:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Disable shadow password functions on OpenHarmony

OpenHarmony does not provide shadow password functions (getspnam, etc.)
which are required by HAVE_SHADOW_H detection in Squid. This patch
disables the shadow password functionality to allow successful compilation.

Signed-off-by: OpenHarmony Build Team <build@openharmony.io>
---
 configure.ac | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -1,8 +1,14 @@
-# Check for shadow password support
-AC_CHECK_HEADERS([shadow.h], [
-  AC_DEFINE(HAVE_SHADOW_H, 1, [Define if you have the <shadow.h> header file.])
-])
+# Check for shadow password support
+# OpenHarmony does not provide shadow password functions
+# Disable HAVE_SHADOW_H to prevent compilation errors
+#
+# AC_CHECK_HEADERS([shadow.h], [
+#   AC_DEFINE(HAVE_SHADOW_H, 1, [Define if you have the <shadow.h> header file.])
+# ])
+AC_MSG_NOTICE([Disabling shadow password support for OpenHarmony])
 
 # Other authentication checks
 AC_CHECK_HEADERS([crypt.h])
-- 
2.25.1

---
**Patch Details:**

**Problem:**
Squid's configure script attempts to detect and use shadow password functions
(getspnam, getspnam_r, etc.) which are not available in OpenHarmony's musl C library.

**Root Cause:**
OpenHarmony uses musl libc which does not implement the shadow password API.
The shadow.h header and related functions are missing.

**Solution:**
Disable the HAVE_SHADOW_H configuration check by commenting out the relevant
AC_CHECK_HEADERS macro in configure.ac.

**Impact:**
- Shadow password authentication will not be available
- Basic authentication and other methods remain functional
- No runtime issues expected for standard proxy use cases

**Testing:**
- Successfully compiled on OpenHarmony aarch64
- Basic proxy functionality verified